{"ref": "Mishnah Arakhin 9:6", "heRef": "משנה ערכין ט׳:ו׳", "sectionRef": "Mishnah Arakhin 9", "indexTitle": "Mishnah Arakhin", "heIndexTitle": "משנה ערכין", "categories": ["Mishnah", "Seder Kodashim"], "next": null, "sectionNames": ["Chapter", "Mishnah"], "versions": [{"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "Mishnah Yomit by Dr. Joshua Kulp", "license": "CC-BY", "versionSource": "http://learn.conservativeyeshiva.org/mishnah/", "text": "A city whose roofs [look as if] they form its wall, Or that was not encompassed by a wall in the days of Joshua ben Nun, is not considered like houses in a walled city. [A house in any of] the following counts a house in a walled city: [those in a city] of no less than three courtyards, having two houses each, which have been encompassed by a wall in the days of Joshua ben Nun, such as the old acroplis of Tzippori, the fort of Gush-Halav, old Yodfat, Gamla, G'dod, Hadid, Ono, Jerusalem and other similar cities."}], "available_versions": [{"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "Torat Emet 357", "license": "Public Domain", "versionSource": "http://www.toratemetfreeware.com/index.html?downloads"}, {"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "Mishnah, ed. Romm, Vilna 1913", "license": "Public Domain", "versionSource": "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001741739"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "William Davidson Edition - English", "license": "CC-BY-NC", "versionSource": "https://korenpub.com/collections/the-noe-edition-koren-talmud-bavli-1"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "Mishnah Yomit by Dr. Joshua Kulp", "license": "CC-BY", "versionSource": "http://learn.conservativeyeshiva.org/mishnah/"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "german", "actualLanguage":